cided this would be a good place to live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T09:48:23-08:00","id":43574,"title":"","content":"It's in the 50s in Boston.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T12:38:17-08:00","id":43660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/43194-who-else-is-freezing?p=43568#post43568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's 20 degrees below Zero outside.<br /> <br /> It is a testament to the insanity of our species that someone decided this would be a good place to live.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great Lakes area? I've always thought they were the nuttiest when it came to that.<br /> <br /> They left places like Norway and crossed an ocean to settle in a place <b>JUST AS DAMN COLD AND INHOSPITABLE AS THE PLACE THEY LEFT!!</b><br /> <br /> Of course, the Irish and English aren't much better. Found someplace just like home, too, only on the other side of the ocean. With all the fun ice storms and nonsense included.<br /> <br /> <br /> The French and the Spanish are the only ones who had the right idea......settled places with milder climates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:27:59-08:00","id":43695,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the French and the Spanish did pretty good. Although the French moved just as far north. The earliest settlements in Indiana are all French (Vincennes being the oldest I believe), and they ruled that entire region for a century before the British took it from them. The Brits only had it for 20 or so years before the Revolutionary War.<br /> <br /> I am working in Vegas at the moment, so I am avoiding the cold weather. My wife and kids are in the Indianapolis area, and they are snowed in. My wife just told me our poor dog went out to use the restroom, and froze up in the snow. My wife had to rescue her because she was shivering and couldn't move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:50:44-08:00","id":43709,"title":"","content":"If I was the kind of person who used emoticons, I would have just now typed, &quot;Awww, doggie )-:&quot;<br /> <br /> But I'm not that person. The sentiment is there, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:05:14-08:00","id":43718,"title":"","content":"Well, it's a record setter cold snap here in Georgia; tomorrow is going to be colder than it has been in the past twenty years. So much so that Gwinnett district supervisor Wilbanks aka. Mr. &quot;Nuclear attack? Keep the schools open. We only close for REAL emergencies.&quot; Is closing the schools tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Good news is my Mom doesn't have to teach tomorrow! And I'm probably going to have go out on business anyway! Isn't that wonderful?<br /> <br /> Stupid windchill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 01-06-2014, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/